<template>
  <div class="page">
    <h1 class="pdx-txt-title">Cascader</h1>
    <p class="pdx-txt-body pdx-ink-muted intro">
      <code>&lt;pdx-cascader&gt;</code> — multi-level drill-down selector.
      Each selection opens the next column of children (Country → Region → City).
      Supports lazy loading, search, disabled nodes, clearable.
    </p>

    <!-- ═══ 1. Basic ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-basic class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-basic>

    <!-- ═══ 2. Pre-selected ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-preselected class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-preselected>

    <!-- ═══ 3. Searchable ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-searchable class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-searchable>

    <!-- ═══ 4. Change on select ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-change-on-select class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-change-on-select>

    <!-- ═══ 5. Disabled items ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-disabled class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-disabled>

    <!-- ═══ Lazy loading ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-lazy class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-lazy>

    <!-- ═══ 6. Custom separator ═══ -->
    <app-demo-comp-cascader-separator class="demo-section"></app-demo-comp-cascader-separator>

    <!-- ═══ Slots ═══ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Slots</h2>
      <div class="options-table">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Scope</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>option</code></td><td><code>{ node, level, selected }</code></td><td>Custom cascader option.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Reference ═══ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Props Reference</h2>
      <div class="options-table">
        <div class="opt-header"><span>Prop</span><span>Type</span><span>Description</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>options</code><span>CascaderNode[]</span><span>Tree of { value, label, children?, disabled? }</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>value</code><span>string[]</span><span>Selected path from root to leaf</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>searchable</code><span>boolean</span><span>Enable search across all levels</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>separator</code><span>string</span><span>Display separator (default: ' / ')</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>changeOnSelect</code><span>boolean</span><span>Allow selecting non-leaf nodes</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>loadChildren</code><span>function</span><span>Lazy load: (node) => Promise&lt;CascaderNode[]&gt;</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>clearable</code><span>boolean</span><span>Show clear button (default: true)</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>disabled</code><span>boolean</span><span>Disabled state</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>placeholder</code><span>string</span><span>Placeholder text</span></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="pdx-txt-subheading" style="margin-top:var(--pdx-space-lg)">Events</h3>
      <div class="options-table">
        <div class="opt-header"><span>Event</span><span>Detail</span><span>Description</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>value-change</code><span>{ value }</span><span>Its model, the path: selection changed; <code>getLabels()</code> gives the labels</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>open-change</code><span>{ value }</span><span>The panel opened (<code>true</code>) or closed (<code>false</code>)</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>pdx-clear</code><span>—</span><span>Value cleared</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>pdx-load-error</code><span>{ node, error }</span><span><code>loadChildren</code> rejected; the branch can be clicked again</span></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="pdx-txt-subheading" style="margin-top:var(--pdx-space-lg)">Methods, states and parts</h3>
      <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
        The panel is driven by the overlay verbs; the path is the model, <code>value</code>. What a theme or a page
        styles on <code>&lt;pdx-cascader&gt;</code>: its custom states on the host and its parts. The classes inside are not public.
      </p>
      <div class="options-table">
        <div class="opt-header"><span>Method, state or part</span><span></span><span>What it is</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>show() / close() / toggle()</code><span></span><span>Open, close, or flip the panel</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>clear() / getLabels()</code><span></span><span>Empty the path; the labels of the path</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>:state(open) / :state(disabled)</code><span></span><span>The panel is open; <code>disabled</code> is set</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>:state(loading)</code><span></span><span>A branch's children are being fetched</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>[data-part="root"] / [data-part="clear"]</code><span></span><span>The trigger; the clear button</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>[data-part="popup"] / [data-part="search"]</code><span></span><span>The panel; its search field</span></div>
        <div class="opt-row"><code>[data-part="list"] / [data-part="option"] / [data-part="spinner"]</code><span></span><span>A column or the results; an option; a branch's spinner</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
@page '/components/cascader';
@title 'Cascader Component';
</script>

<style scoped>
  .page { }
</style>
